# item: Chromium is the browser (2026-10-21). On the Duo's hybris stack
# only Chromium draws with the GPU: its GPU process reaches the Adreno
# through hybris' EGL (WebGL at 26 fps where WebKit paints on the CPU), and
# it speaks text-input v3, so item's keyboard rises for its fields. The
# port's phosh keeps GNOME Web (adaptation/system/phosh-mimeapps.list).
# Read for the desktop "item" (XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=item:GNOME) before
# gnome-mimeapps.list, which puts Firefox first - and Firefox's hidden
# entry has no Exec, so a link opened nothing (the Agent's login,
# 2026-10-21). A user's own choice in ~/.config wins. Chromium's flags
# (the Wayland socket, text-input v3) are in item-chromium, installed as
# /etc/chromium.d/item.
[Default Applications]
x-scheme-handler/http=chromium.desktop
x-scheme-handler/https=chromium.desktop
text/html=chromium.desktop
application/xhtml+xml=chromium.desktop
